sted in Jordan in connection with an attack on a Greek Orthodox church last week. The arrests took place following a dawn shootout with security forces during which the suspects were wounded.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Union slams Audi CEO for joining Trump at campaign rally, while Chancellor Merz and President Steinmeier embark on separate Asia tours</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c141913aca92f439b3eb27e3fd4f6531c553e4d912b70a981bf379b138b7d27d</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-union-slams-audi-ceo-for-joining-trump-at-campaign-rally-while-chancellor-merz-and-pres/live-79760097--fec78f9e2107.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-union-slams-audi-ceo-for-joining-trump-at-campaign-rally-while-chancellor-merz-and-president-steinmeier-embark-on-separate-asia-tours/live-79760097?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Audi's boss is facing a backlash in Germany after appearing alongside Donald Trump at a campaign rally. Meanwhile, Germany's chancellor and president are heading to Asia on separate diplomatic missions. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela: Opposition leader Machado returns from exile, received by thousands of supporters in Caracas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71bbda617e9bdb8ad65ebf989d3a2352ecc7f3bb8a286a4b1fd82331165d7aa0</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:19:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venezuela-opposition-leader-machado-returns-from-exile-received-by-thousands-of-supporters-in-caraca/a-79759187--b210bf37f8c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-opposition-leader-machado-returns-from-exile-received-by-thousands-of-supporters-in-caracas/a-79759187?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nobel Peach Prize winner and popular Venezuelan political opposition figure Maria Corina Machado has returned from nearly a year in exile. She was greeted by thousands of cheering supporters in Caracas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>From rotten food to political opponents: Researchers explore how disgust relates to our beliefs, and why the connection is complicated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1aa0cf0843af6b8fcda592808e899282c1999c8386717a22dd3fc1e406970f</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:19:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-w/a-79734659--e9b7cd7e436d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-why-the-connection-is-complicated/a-79734659?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some studies have linked disgust sensitivity to socially conservative attitudes. But ahead of the US midterm elections, does disgust shape our politics, or do our beliefs shape what we find disgusting?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Remark on Modi's father stirs political row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e643c539b022845029e5f11883fb221ae4cd2176517b2115f4560047c6634375</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:19:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T07:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-remark-on-modi-s-father-stirs-political-row/live-79758965--7e6cacdc5195.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-remark-on-modi-s-father-stirs-political-row/live-79758965?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An opposition leader's impromptu remark concerning PM Modi is causing a political stir in India with the ruling party now planning a protest. Also, the prince of Liechtenstein is in Mumbai.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia election: Vucic concedes defeat to student-led movement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3afb6ce2f244449138b794e7727fc1a2e80bbe9dcd46eb27fc64875ddb03e590</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T21:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-election-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-student-led-movement/a-79753482--f6c996d88fe7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-election-vucic-concedes-defeat-to-student-led-movement/a-79753482?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a seismic political shift, Serbia's longtime strongman leader Aleksandar Vucic has conceded defeat to a student-led opposition movement in the country's parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Protein shakes for teenagers: Good or bad idea?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad9bcfb59d5036d4697affd7445dc044501926b7b4964f9b52ebc2ce2a9721f8</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/protein-shakes-for-teenagers-good-or-bad-idea/a-79751929--869a08ab5ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/protein-shakes-for-teenagers-good-or-bad-idea/a-79751929?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protein products are marketed as a way of building muscle and losing weight — and they're very popular with young people. They also claim to promote healthy growth in children. Is this true? How much protein is healthy?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda says it has no active Ebola cases, but infections in Kenya and Nigeria are prompting fresh scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85b05148fe9d66fcec28e83974135e2866e5a53849f839c31ffd863a6644152a</id><updated>2026-10-26T15:18:15Z</update